---
import { projects } from "../../data/projects";
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";

const project = projects.find((entry) => entry.slug === "objekt-tcg");

if (!project) {
  throw new Error("Missing project data for objekt-tcg");
}

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<ProjectLayout project={project}>
  <p>
    objekt-tcg is a sibling project to <a href="https://objekt.my" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">objekt.my</a>,
    cloned from its foundation and then pushed in a different direction: instead of trades and
    lists, it's a TCG-style pack opening game for Cosmo objekt collectors. It's abandoned now, but
    it was never really meant to ship — it was an excuse to spend time with real-time 3D rendering
    in the browser.
  </p>

  <h2>The idea</h2>
  <p>
    Where objekt.my derives ownership live from a blockchain indexer, this app owned ownership
    itself: users could open a free pack once an hour, the server rolled the cards, and the result
    was persisted to its own database. The indexer was only ever read as a catalog for card
    images and metadata, borrowing the same Next.js, Drizzle/PostgreSQL, Better Auth, and Redis
    foundation as objekt.my, but with its own database and its own Discord OAuth app.
  </p>

  <h2>What actually got built</h2>
  <p>
    Most of the work went into the pack itself: a scrubbable pack-opening animation built with
    React Three Fiber and Three.js, rendering real <code>.glb</code> models with customizable
    packs and stickers rather than a flat 2D reveal. That 3D layer is the part that ended up being
    the actual point of the project.
  </p>

  <h2>Why it stopped</h2>
  <p>
    It stayed a solo experiment rather than a real spinoff — worth keeping around as a record of
    playing with a rendering stack outside the usual web app work, not as a live product.
  </p>

  <p class="note-box">
    The source repository is private, and there's no live deployment.
  </p>

  <figure>
    <img
      class="frame-image"
      src={`${base}assets/screenshots/objekt-tcg-pack.png`}
      alt="Screenshot of the objekt-tcg pack-opening scene: a rendered TRIPLES pack from the Atom02 Premier set, ready to be torn open."
    />
    <figcaption>
      The pack-opening scene, from a local dev run — this is a still frame of what's normally a
      scrubbable 3D animation.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</ProjectLayout>
